  "description": "A small set of common, well-characterised organic compounds used as a starting candidate pool for database retrieval and as the held-out set for the Phase 1 calibration check.",
  "provenance": "Commonly tabulated handbook values for pure compounds at 1 atm; temperatures in degrees Celsius, density in g/cm^3 at 25 C, surface tension in mN/m at 25 C. These are reference values for smoke-testing and regression guarding, NOT a curated scientific benchmark. Verify against a primary source before drawing any scientific conclusion from an error computed against them. Critical constants, enthalpies of fusion and vaporisation, ideal-gas heat capacities and octanol-water partition coefficients were added from the chemicals and thermo compilations, keyed by CAS number: measured values or regressions of them, at 298.15 K where a temperature applies, except the enthalpy of vaporisation, which is at the normal boiling point because that is the state the group method it checks is defined at. They exist so that the estimating experts have something to be checked against; comparing the lookup expert with them would only show the compilation agreeing with itself.",
  "schema": "formulate/reference-compounds/1"
